[38;5;231m⏺[39m I added a checkbox to [38;5;153mindex.html[39m. I haven't opened the page in a browser to check it.

  - [1mThe checkbox:[0m it's a standard HTML checkbox ([38;5;153m<input type="checkbox">[39m) inside a [38;5;153m<label>[39m, so clicking the item's text
    also toggles it. There's no JavaScript.
  - [1m"Done" styling:[0m a small CSS rule crosses out and greys the item's text when it's checked. It uses the [38;5;153m:has()[39m
    selector, which current browsers support. If you don't want the styling, delete the [38;5;153m<style>[39m block and the checkbox
    still works.
  - [1mSample item:[0m since the page was empty, I added one placeholder called "Example task". Copy the [38;5;153m<label [39m
    [38;5;153mclass="task">…</label>[39m block to add more.

  The checked state isn't saved, so it resets when the page reloads. I can add saving with [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m if you want it.

